>6. A Three-Item Nightstand</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#7-anchor-tall-furniture">7. Anchor Tall Furniture</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#8-cube-shelves-with-fabric-bins">8. Cube Shelves With Fabric Bins</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#storage-you-already-have">Storage You Already Have</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#9-the-space-under-the-bed">9. The Space Under the Bed</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#10-the-back-of-the-door">10. The Back of the Door</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#11-shelves-above-eye-level">11. Shelves Above Eye Level</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#make-room-for-what-you-love">Make Room for What You Love</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#12-a-reading-or-hobby-corner">12. A Reading or Hobby Corner</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#13-a-clear-desk-zone">13. A Clear Desk Zone</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#keep-your-room-organized">Keep Your Room Organized</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#14-a-10minute-daily-reset">14. A 10-Minute Daily Reset</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#15-one-in-one-out">15. One In, One Out</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#mistakes-to-avoid-when-you-organize-your-room">Mistakes to Avoid When You Organize Your Room</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#room-organization-faq">Room Organization FAQ</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#where-do-i-start-when-my-room-is-a-mess">Where do I start when my room is a mess?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-long-does-it-take-to-organize-a-room">How long does it take to organize a room?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-do-i-organize-a-small-room-with-no-closet">How do I organize a small room with no closet?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-do-i-keep-my-room-organized">How do I keep my room organized?</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#final-thoughts">Final Thoughts</a></li></ul></div></nav>


<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Start With Zones</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Every bedroom does a few jobs: sleeping, getting dressed, relaxing and sometimes working or studying. When each job has its own area, the things that belong to it stay there. Clothes live in the dressing zone, books in the relax zone and papers in the work zone, and nothing needs to sit on the bed.</p>



