" y="514" font-size="21" fill="#342E2A">other rooms</text><rect x="758" y="540" width="26" height="26" rx="6" fill="#DCE5D6" stroke="#8FA689" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M764,553 l6,7 l10,-13" fill="none" stroke="#C85A32" stroke-width="3"/><text x="1112" y="562" font-size="18" fill="#6E645C" text-anchor="end">2 min</text><text x="800" y="562" font-size="21" fill="#342E2A">Clear the floor</text><line x1="758" y1="620" x2="1112" y2="620" stroke="#D8CBBB" stroke-width="2"/><text x="758" y="655" font-size="19" font-weight="700" fill="#C85A32">Total: about 10 minutes</text><rect x="60" y="730" width="1080" height="100" rx="14" fill="#DCE5D6" stroke="#8FA689" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="60" y="730" width="10" height="100" rx="5" fill="#8FA689"/><text x="96" y="771" font-size="20" fill="#342E2A"><tspan font-weight="700">Tip:</tspan> the Sleep Foundation suggests spending a few minutes each day picking</text><text x="96" y="805" font-size="20" fill="#342E2A">up clutter so it does not build up and feel overwhelming.</text><text x="60" y="872" font-size="15" fill="#6E645C">Daily pick-up tip: Sleep Foundation. Zone plan, checklist and timings: our recommendation.</text></svg><figcaption>A simple bedroom zone plan with a 10-minute daily reset checklist.</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A tidy room can also help you wind down. The Sleep Foundation’s guide on <a href="https://www.sleepfoundation.org/bedroom-environment/how-to-design-the-ideal-bedroom-for-sleep" target="_blank" rel="noopener">how to set up a bedroom for better sleep</a> notes that visual clutter can generate stress, a known barrier to quality sleep, and suggests reviewing the items you do not really need and spending just a few minutes each day picking up clutter so it does not build up.</p>



