<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How to Organize Your Room in 7 Steps</h2>



<ol class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Set a timer and clear the bed.</strong> Start with the bed so you have a clean surface to sort on. Work in 25-minute rounds with short breaks.</li>


<li><strong>Sort with four boxes.</strong> Label them keep, donate, trash and belongs elsewhere. Pick up every item from the floor, chair and surfaces and drop it in a box.</li>


<li><strong>Do the clothes first.</strong> Dirty clothes go in the hamper, clean ones get folded or hung, and anything that no longer fits goes in the donate box.</li>


<li><strong>Clear the surfaces.</strong> Empty the dresser, nightstand and desk, wipe them down and put back only what you use every day.</li>


<li><strong>Check hidden spots.</strong> Look under the bed, in the closet and in drawers for things you forgot you had.</li>


<li><strong>Give everything a zone.</strong> Put each item in the zone where you use it, in a bin, drawer or on a hook.</li>


<li><strong>Empty the boxes right away.</strong> Take donations to the car, trash outside and return belongs-elsewhere items to their rooms the same day.</li>
</ol>



